---

Why this and not MIT.

PickFrame is a running commercial SaaS. A permissive licence would allow
anyone to run it as a competing service, and that decision cannot be
undone once made: code released under MIT stays available under MIT for
everyone who already has a copy.

A source-available notice costs nothing for the purpose this repository
serves — being read — while leaving the commercial question closed.

If the intent later changes to genuine open source, replacing this file
with a standard licence text is a one-file change. Going the other
direction is not.
